पार्थ नैवेह नामुत्र विनाशस्तस्य विद्यते ।
न हि कल्याणकृत्कश्चिद्दुर्गतिं तात गच्छति ॥ ४० ॥\"}]},{\"section\":\"verse_text\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.verse-text\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2015,\"bb\":1783,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/40/b1783/\",\"body_value\":\"śrī-bhagavān uvāca
pārtha naiveha nāmutra
vināśas tasya vidyate
na hi kalyāṇa-kṛt kaścid
durgatiṁ tāta gacchati\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":2016,\"bb\":1784,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/40/b1784/\",\"shadow_value\":\"śrī-bhagavān uvāca – the Supreme Personality of Godhead said; pārtha – O son of Pṛthā; na eva – never is it so; iha – in this material world; na – never; amutra – in the next life; vināśaḥ – destruction; tasya – his; vidyate – exists; na – never; hi – certainly; kalyāṇa-kṛt – one who is engaged in auspicious activities; kaścit – anyone; durgatim – to degradation; tāta – My friend; gacchati – goes.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"śrī-bhagavān uvāca\",\"translation\":\"the Supreme Personality of Godhead said\"},{\"word\":\"pārtha\",\"translation\":\"O son of Pṛthā\"},{\"word\":\"na eva\",\"translation\":\"never is it so\"},{\"word\":\"iha\",\"translation\":\"in this material world\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"amutra\",\"translation\":\"in the next life\"},{\"word\":\"vināśaḥ\",\"translation\":\"destruction\"},{\"word\":\"tasya\",\"translation\":\"his\"},{\"word\":\"vidyate\",\"translation\":\"exists\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"hi\",\"translation\":\"certainly\"},{\"word\":\"kalyāṇa-kṛt\",\"translation\":\"one who is engaged in auspicious activities\"},{\"word\":\"kaścit\",\"translation\":\"anyone\"},{\"word\":\"durgatim\",\"translation\":\"to degradation\"},{\"word\":\"tāta\",\"translation\":\"My friend\"},{\"word\":\"gacchati\",\"translation\":\"goes\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":2017,\"bb\":1785,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/40/b1785/\",\"body_value\":\"The Supreme Personality of Godhead said: Son of Pṛthā, a transcendentalist engaged in auspicious activities does not meet with destruction either in this world or in the spiritual world; one who does good, My friend, is never overcome by evil.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2018,\"bb\":1786,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/40/b1786/\",\"body_value\":\"In the Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam (1.5.17) Śrī Nārada Muni instructs Vyāsadeva as follows:\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"verse_text\",\"id\":2019,\"bb\":1787,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/40/b1787/\",\"body_value\":\"tyaktvā sva-dharmaṁ caraṇāmbujaṁ harer
bhajann apakvo ’tha patet tato yadi
yatra kva vābhadram abhūd amuṣya kiṁ
ko vārtha āpto ’bhajatāṁ sva-dharmataḥ\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2020,\"bb\":1788,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/40/b1788/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2021,\"bb\":1789,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/40/b1789/\",\"body_value\":\"The purport may be understood as follows. Humanity may be divided into two sections, namely, the regulated and the nonregulated. Those who are engaged simply in bestial sense gratifications without knowledge of their next life or spiritual salvation belong to the nonregulated section. And those who follow the principles of prescribed duties in the scriptures are classified amongst the regulated section. The nonregulated section, both civilized and noncivilized, educated and noneducated, strong and weak, are full of animal propensities. Their activities are never auspicious, because while enjoying the animal propensities of eating, sleeping, defending and mating, they perpetually remain in material existence, which is always miserable. On the other hand, those who are regulated by scriptural injunctions, and who thus rise gradually to Kṛṣṇa consciousness, certainly progress in life.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":2022,\"bb\":1790,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/6/40/b1790/\",\"body_value\":\"$26\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 6.40\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 6.40\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2b:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n31:I[78455,[\"/_next/static